Z||000000||drednot||05-23-2001||08:19 PM||||Ok, here is what is going on.  about 1 week ago I noticed my engine starting to have pulsating rhymic idling.  it was sort of going weerrrReeerWeerrReeeeeWeeeeReeeeeeWeeeeee... and so on.  It had a variance of about 200 rpms.  it did not start doing this all at once, it just sort of crept up on me.  now it is doing this at all speeds, and it is effecting derivability.  it feels sort of like one cylinder is causing engine breaking, and all the others are working.  when I hit the gas, I still have full power though.  I replaced the spark plugs and wires.  no effect.  today, after a 30 mile highway trip @ 85+ mph, the car has a whole different sound to it.  the engine does not sound like a fiero anymore, more like a old Chrysler!!  check engine light coming on and off.  I opened the trunk and listened closely to the engine while it was idling, and it is making a ticking sound, sort of like a loose gear sound.  what do you all think?  can I save it??  btw, it is a 1985 4 cyl||||reg||11
